__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/

# Corpora and derived artifacts: large, regenerable, never versioned.
#
# 🔴 ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH, and that is load-bearing. An unanchored
# `data/` matches ANY directory named `data` at any depth. It did, for both
# `src/rsr/data/` (the synthetic-corpus package, gauntlet 2.5) and
# `third_party/ThoughtGestaltCode/tg/data/` (five files of the pinned
# reference). Both were invisible from the scaffold commit until 2026-09-17:
# ignored files do not show in `git status`, `git add -A` skips them silently,
# and every local test passes because the files are on disk. A fresh clone had
# `tests/test_synthetic.py` with nothing to import, and a vendored tree that did
# not match the pin.
#
# `tests/test_repo_integrity.py` now checks the class, not the two instances.
/data/
/outputs/
*.ckpt
*.pt

# ...but the measurement ledgers are evidence, not output.
#
# `/runs/` correctly ignores checkpoints (binary, large, regenerable) and
# heartbeats (per-step, chatty). It also ignored `runs/<id>/ledger.json`, which is
# the artefact the overnight protocol requires **every reported number to trace
# to** -- so a cycle's evidence could not be committed and a claim had nothing
# durable behind it. Un-ignore the ledgers and the writeups only; the directory
# itself must stay ignored or `git add -A` sweeps in the .pt files.
# Note the form: `/runs/**` ignores the CONTENTS, and `!/runs/**/` re-includes the
# directories. Ignoring `/runs/` itself would make the negations below dead letters
# -- git does not descend into an excluded directory, so a re-include under one can
# never match. That is exactly the trap this rule was in.
/runs/**
!/runs/**/
!/runs/**/ledger.json
# The frozen config a ledger's `config_hash` hashes. The hash is in the ledger and
# the ledger is committed; without the manifest beside it the hash has nothing to
# be checked against, which is the same gap the ledger rule closed one level up.
!/runs/**/manifest.json
!/runs/**/RESULTS.md
!/runs/**/walls.json
!/runs/**/baseline.json
# 🔴 ...and the RAW measurement JSON a ledger row was read out of.
#
# A ledger row's `how` field names the artefact it came from -- that is the whole
# point of the field: "go and look at that artefact instead of trusting the row."
# `/runs/**` ignored every one of them. Committing S0-02's ledger left all five
# `how` fields pointing at `capture_cost.json`, `e0c_fifo_with_bridge.json` and
# `mutations.json`, none of which a fresh clone has -- and `git add -A` skipped
# them in silence, which is the exact failure mode the `/data/` note above
# describes. `runs/cycle-01-masked-loss/{gates,raw}.json` were already lost the
# same way.
#
# `.jsonl` heartbeats stay ignored (per-step, chatty) and so do `.pt` and `.log`.
!/runs/**/*.json
# Scratch counters written by the test harness are not evidence: `RSR_TEST_COUNT`
# and `mutation_battery.SCRATCH_COUNT` both land under `runs/` as dotfiles.
/runs/.*.json
/runs/**/.*.json

# Belt and braces: the source packages are never ignorable, whatever pattern
# comes back. Scoped to sources so `__pycache__/` above still applies.
!src/rsr/data/
!src/rsr/data/*.py
!third_party/ThoughtGestaltCode/tg/data/
!third_party/ThoughtGestaltCode/tg/data/*.py

# Golden tensors ARE versioned (tests/fixtures/*.npz) -- they are the external
# claim test_fidelity.py rests on. See ADR-0002.

# The per-run test census written by tests/conftest.py (gauntlet 1.3).
test-count.json

# The orchestrator's runtime state (scripts/orchestrator/). Machine-local and
# rewritten every tick: locks, logs, state (night.json, pipeline.json, spend.jsonl,
# notified.json), claude session records and their output, slot job records, the
# HALT switch and the queue file. `.orchestrator/outbox/` and
# `.orchestrator/cycle-protocol.md` stay TRACKED -- the outbox is the researcher's
# report channel and the protocol is what every manager cycle reads.
/.orchestrator/locks/
/.orchestrator/logs/
/.orchestrator/state/
/.orchestrator/cycles/
/.orchestrator/jobs/
/.orchestrator/HALT
/.orchestrator/queue.json
# Per-item worktrees and the manager's (`.worktrees/<item>`, `.worktrees/_mgr`).
/.worktrees/
